Update are near-duplicate forms. Dashboard.jsx's Edit Profile button opens ProfileUpdate, while Profile.jsx's own Edit-profile button opens ProfileCompletion instead. Separately, Profile.jsx and Dashboard.jsx use different conditions (checkMissingFields vs hasCompletedProfile flag) to decide whether to auto-show the completion modal, so a user could satisfy one check and not the other."}, {"id": "hyperedge_two_public_profile_pages", "label": "Two overlapping public 'view a profile' pages, one of them unrouted", "relation": "duplicate_implementation_pattern", "nodes": ["onboarding_profile_profile_jsx", "onboarding_profile_userprofile_jsx", "clubs_clubcard", "onboarding_profile_clubendpoints_details", "onboarding_profile_userendpoints_details"], "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/specs/onboarding-profile.md", "description": "Profile.jsx (routed at /user/:userName and /club/:userName, fetches via clubEndpoints.details, linked to from ClubCard) and UserProfile.jsx (visually more developed, fetches via userEndpoints.details, but has no route in routesConfig.jsx and relies on a cookie that's never set) both implement a 'view someone's profile' page; the spec treats UserProfile.jsx as a work-in-progress replacement rather than an active page."}]}